WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.180
It really is the White House that was supposedly
going to be all about transparency and openness

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.820
and, uh, keeping the American people informed
and part of the communication about what they're

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:17.400
doing has now gone six months without holding
a traditional press briefing.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.089
There's been a different press secretary.

00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:23.720
Uh, there is a different press secretary in
place now than six months ago, but it has

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:29.119
been six full months and there is no sign
that the White House is going to resume these

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:30.119
press briefings.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:35.500
And part of the problem is probably that the
current press secretary wouldn't be able to

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.250
handle press briefings.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.500
Her name is Stephanie Grisham.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.250
She replaced, of course, Sarah Huckabee Sanders.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:47.120
When Sanders left and recently Stephanie Grisham
put out a statement answering questions about

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.820
why, why are there no press briefings and
this is genius in the sense that it is evil

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.850
disinformation genius.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:59.809
They are indirectly referring to Twitter to
excuse not having press briefings.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:02.040
Check this out and look at the language that's
used.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:07.009
Quote, this is White House Press Secretary
Stephanie Grisham to ABC News.

00:01:07.009 --> 00:01:10.960
President Trump communicates directly with
the American people more than any president

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:11.960
in history.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:17.490
The fact that the White House press core can
no longer grand stand on TV is of no concern

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.490
to us.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.400
She's essentially saying Trump speaks directly
to the American people.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.259
She means Twitter, right?

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:30.149
And thus we don't even really need press briefings
where of course reporters get to ask, ask

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:32.610
questions and sometimes call lies out.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.040
Instead Trump goes on Twitter where it is
one way communication with Trump blocking

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.229
detractors on Twitter, people he doesn't like
and no opportunity for serious follow ups

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:44.969
from actual journalists.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:50.829
That is what they are using to defend, not
having a press briefing in six months despite

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:56.950
claiming both before and during the presidency
that they are the most open and transparent

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.759
administration in history, which of course
only an idiot or someone can go a consistently

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:08.050
and persistently misinformed would ever fall
for and what's happening is that Grisham really

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:12.200
can't handle what it is that would happen
during a press briefing.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.670
Aside from not even doing the briefings.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.790
She also has done barely any interviews.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:23.140
I'm aware of only one that she did with that
right wing TV station ownership groups, Sinclair

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:28.650
broadcast group, and specifically the interviewer
was that right-wing commentator Eric Bolling.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.110
I don't even get what she's doing to earn
her salary.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:35.140
She's not talking to the press in press briefings.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.430
She's barely doing interviews.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.330
I don't even really understand the point.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.580
And of course, part of the explanation that
the press briefings are merely something that

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:48.330
allowed the press corps, which they've characterized
as just liberal, which is of course not true,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.780
that it's merely a venue for the press corps
to grandstand.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.870
This is another authoritarian tendency.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.200
It's part of the presses bad.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.230
Letting the press asks questions is bad.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:05.040
Instead we are going to do one way communication
which is reminiscent of the endless speeches

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.870
of the despotic dictators.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.230
The world over ranging from, you know, we
don't have to mention the German guy but we

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:17.680
can just go more recently Castro would just
do one way communication, uh, the Chavez Maduro

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.430
duo [inaudible] loves one way communication
with no opportunity for challenging and pushing

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.330
back against what's being said.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:30.610
This is a hallmark of those with authoritarian
tendencies and this is actually particularly

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:36.730
of concern because it actually might set a
new standard or a new expectation even for

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:37.770
future presidents.

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:43.550
There would be, I'm hoping future presidents
that don't have the anti media authoritarian

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:48.170
tendencies of Donald Trump that don't share
his disdain for the press.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:53.670
But if we go, not six months but another year
and a half up until the next inauguration,

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:59.840
if Trump loses, that would be two years of
no press briefings or almost no press briefings.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:03.820
It may start to seem like the norm even for
future presidents.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.970
I hope that that's not the case, but that
is a concern.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.310
The most transparent administration in history,
right?

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:16.060
All they do is lie and obfuscate and then
canceled a few opportunities that even exist

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:23.449
to ask questions about those lies and obfuscations
and they defend it with, well, Trump's tweeting,

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:28.159
he's communicating directly with the American
people, so it's all fine.

00:04:28.159 --> 00:04:33.219
This is the authoritarian slide that we've
been talking about for years at this point.

